# Architecture

Source of truth: `AGENTS.md` sections 4, 5, 10 and `docs/adr/`.

## Dependency direction (enforced by pnpm, `exports`, tsconfig and ESLint)

```
core    -> nothing internal (pure libs only: immer, zod)
content -> core (TYPES ONLY) + zod + jsonc-parser
game    -> core, content
tools   -> core, content
```

- `core` defines the types it consumes (`ContentDb`, `Balance`); `content` imports them (ADR 0003).
- Import packages only by name (`@mangaka/core`). Deep imports are impossible (`exports: { ".": ... }`).
- `game` reaches the host only through `PlatformApi` (ADR 0008). UI sends commands, never mutates state.

## Working rules

- Never bypass a boundary to go faster. If a rule blocks you, say so and propose an alternative.
- Every important decision gets an ADR in `docs/adr/` (context, decision, alternatives, consequences). ADRs are immutable: supersede, do not edit.
- Plan before coding any non-trivial task; wait for Hugo when it involves architecture or game design.
- Do not implement v1/v2 features (AGENTS.md 3). Design so they fit later, without speculative abstractions.
- Do not add a dependency without checking the registry (existence, last release, licence, size) and the 3-day release-age policy (ADR 0013).
- At the end of a task: update `docs/PROGRESS.md`, summarise done / remaining / points for Hugo to validate.
